    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Why these panels may be empty",
      "description": "Instrumented-but-inactive metrics, and metrics with no instrument.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 43
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Expected to be empty on a freshly started stack.**\n\nEvery query on this dashboard targets a metric that *is* instrumented in production code but was **not observed** during Phase 33.3 verification, because the prefix-update and custom-route DNS code paths did not execute in the sampled window:\n\n- `irandirect_prefix_checks_total`, `irandirect_prefix_check_duration_milliseconds_*`\n- `irandirect_dns_lookups_total`, `irandirect_dns_lookup_duration_milliseconds_*`\n\nThese panels populate once a prefix update check or a custom-route DNS refresh runs. Empty panels here mean *no activity*, not a broken query.\n\n**Not shown at all:** `irandirect.prefix.known_count`, `irandirect.dns.cache_record_count` and `irandirect.prefix.consecutive_failures` have **no instrument** in production code, so no panel is provided.\n\n**Cache-state distribution is omitted.** The `cache_state` label does not appear on any live series. Per the phase brief, deriving it from traces is out of scope, so no fresh/stale/miss panel is included."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "text",
